WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.830
The Human Genome Project
ran from 1990 to 2003.

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.770
It read about 3 billion base pairs.

3
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:14.830
In 2001, sequencing one human-sized genome
cost an estimated 95 million dollars.

4
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.330
By 2022, it cost 525 dollars.

5
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.240
A human genome now takes about a day.

6
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.110
So now that reading a
genome is quick and cheap,

7
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.560
what can we do with it?

8
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.640
In this mission, you'll see how millions
of short fragments are read at the same

9
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.460
time, then assembled by computer.

10
00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:38.010
Then you'll meet the genomes read since,
from crops and a mosquito to extinct

11
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.270
Neanderthals.

12
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:44.040
Your mission: find out what quick,
cheap genome sequencing lets us do.
